Runtime option --xex_patch: the guest path of the XEX patch to apply to the main module.

The runtime applies default.xexp from next to default.xex. A port that ships a title update as a second recompiled
executable has to apply it from a folder of its own (mounted as update: through --update_data_root): the base build
shares the game folder and must never see the patch, and the game folder stays as the player installed it. With
--xex_patch set, that file is the patch and a missing file fails the load. A patch file is never given a patch of its
own, which an override would otherwise make it look up in turn. Unset, nothing changes.

